From: Bernhard Rosenkränzer <bero@lindev.ch>
Subject: Build memstore as a static library

os is a static library and links memstore, which links os back.
With BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON, memstore becomes a shared library and
CMake 4 rejects that cycle. Cycles among static libraries are
allowed. memstore is not installed as its own library.

diff -up a/src/os/memstore/CMakeLists.txt b/src/os/memstore/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/src/os/memstore/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/os/memstore/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 include(CheckCXXCompilerFlag)
 
-add_library(memstore
+add_library(memstore STATIC
   MemStore.cc)
 target_link_libraries(memstore PRIVATE os)
 check_cxx_compiler_flag("-Wno-maybe-uninitialized"
